Package: platformd-attestd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, systemd (>= 257)
Suggests: platformd-attestd-viewer, platformd-trustd, platformd-verifyd
Description: broker for application-requested platform attestation
 platformd-attestd connects a local application to an administrator-approved
 remote verifier. A protected read requires platformd-trustd for TPM
 attestation and platformd-verifyd for contextual user verification.
 The broker socket is not enabled or started on installation.

Package: platformd-attestd-viewer
Section: utils
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, platformd-attestd (= ${binary:Version})
Description: GTK viewer for an attestation-protected document
 View a plain text document from the approved verifier through
 platformd-attestd. The viewer does not save the document to disk.
